### 1.5 Animation and Motion System

```
/* === EASING CURVES === */
--ease-default: cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 0.2, 1);      /* General transitions */
--ease-in: cubic-bezier(0.4, 0, 1, 1);               /* Elements exiting */
--ease-out: cubic-bezier(0, 0, 0.2, 1);               /* Elements entering */
--ease-spring: cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1);     /* Playful bounces */
--ease-smooth: cubic-bezier(0.25, 0.1, 0.25, 1);      /* Smooth, premium feel */

/* === DURATION === */
--duration-instant: 75ms;      /* Micro-interactions: checkbox, toggle */
--duration-fast: 150ms;        /* Hover states, button feedback */
--duration-normal: 200ms;      /* Dropdowns, tooltips */
--duration-moderate: 300ms;    /* Modals, drawers, accordions */
--duration-slow: 500ms;        /* Page transitions, large layout shifts */
--duration-slower: 700ms;      /* Complex animations, chart renders */

/* === ANIMATION PATTERNS (use Framer Motion) === */

// Page enter
{ initial: { opacity: 0, y: 20 }, animate: { opacity: 1, y: 0 }, transition: { duration: 0.4, ease: [0.25, 0.1, 0.25, 1] } }

// Stagger children (for card grids, list items)
{ parent: { staggerChildren: 0.06, delayChildren: 0.1 }, child: { initial: { opacity: 0, y: 12 }, animate: { opacity: 1, y: 0 } } }

// Stat number count-up (dashboard KPIs — animate from 0 to value)
Use Framer Motion's useMotionValue + useTransform + animate to count numbers from 0

// Sidebar expand/collapse
{ layout: true, transition: { type: "spring", stiffness: 300, damping: 30 } }

// Modal enter
{ initial: { opacity: 0, scale: 0.95, y: 10 }, animate: { opacity: 1, scale: 1, y: 0 }, transition: { duration: 0.2, ease: [0, 0, 0.2, 1] } }

// Toast notification slide-in
{ initial: { opacity: 0, x: 100 }, animate: { opacity: 1, x: 0 }, exit: { opacity: 0, x: 100 } }

// Chart data entrance
{ initial: { pathLength: 0 }, animate: { pathLength: 1 }, transition: { duration: 1.2, ease: "easeInOut" } }

// Skeleton loading pulse
{ animate: { opacity: [0.5, 1, 0.5] }, transition: { duration: 1.5, repeat: Infinity, ease: "easeInOut" } }

// Hover card lift
{ whileHover: { y: -2, shadow: "var(--shadow-lg)" }, transition: { duration: 0.2 } }

// Button press
{ whileTap: { scale: 0.98 }, transition: { duration: 0.1 } }
```

### 1.6 Component Design Standards

Every component must follow these patterns:

**Buttons:**
- Primary: Brand-500 bg, white text, brand shadow on hover, scale(0.98) on press
- Secondary: White bg, gray-200 border, gray-700 text, gray-50 bg on hover
- Ghost: Transparent bg, brand-500 text, brand-50 bg on hover
- Destructive: Error-500 bg, white text
- All buttons: 40px height (default), 36px (small), 44px (large), radius-md, font-medium, px-4
- Loading state: Spinner icon replacing text, reduced opacity
- Disabled: opacity-50, cursor-not-allowed, no hover effects

**Input Fields:**
- 40px height, radius-md, gray-200 border, 1px
- Focus: brand-500 border (2px), brand-50 ring (3px offset)
- Error: error-500 border, error-50 background, error message below in text-sm
- Label above in text-sm font-medium gray-700, required asterisk in error-500
- Helper text in text-sm gray-500

**Cards:**
- White bg, radius-lg, shadow-sm, 1px gray-100 border
- Hover: shadow-md, translateY(-2px) transition
- Padding: 24px
- Header: flex between title (text-lg semibold) and actions
- Never stack more than 3 vertical content sections without visual separation

**Tables:**
- Header: gray-50 bg, text-xs uppercase tracking-wide font-semibold gray-500
- Rows: 52px height, hover:gray-50 bg, border-b gray-100
- Checkbox column: 48px wide
- Action column: right-aligned, icon buttons only (not text links)
- Pagination: bottom-right, showing "1-10 of 234" with prev/next
- Empty state: centered illustration + message + CTA button
- Loading state: skeleton rows (6 rows of animated pulse bars)

**Modals:**
- Backdrop: black/50 opacity, blur(4px)
- Container: white bg, radius-xl, shadow-xl, max-width based on content (sm:440px, md:560px, lg:720px, xl:960px)
- Header: px-6 py-4, border-b, title + close button
- Body: px-6 py-4, scrollable if content exceeds viewport
- Footer: px-6 py-4, border-t, right-aligned buttons

**Badges/Tags:**
- Pill shape (radius-full), px-2.5 py-0.5
- Status badges: colored dot (8px circle) + text
- Use semantic colors: success for active/approved, warning for pending, error for overdue/rejected, info for in-progress

**Avatars:**
- Circular, sizes: 24px, 32px, 40px, 48px, 64px
- Fallback: initials on gradient background (use name hash to pick consistent gradient)
- Group: overlapping with -8px margin, +N counter at end
- Online indicator: 10px green dot at bottom-right

**Empty States:**
- Centered in container
- Light illustration (SVG, use brand colors at 20% opacity)
- Heading: text-lg semibold gray-700
- Description: text-sm gray-500, max-w-sm, text-center
- CTA: Primary button

**Loading States:**
- Skeleton screens that mirror the actual layout (not a centered spinner)
- Pulse animation on skeleton elements
- Progressive loading: show structure immediately, fill data as it arrives

**Error States:**
- Inline errors: red border on field + error message below
- Page errors: centered message with retry button
- Toast errors: slide-in from top-right, auto-dismiss after 5s, manual dismiss
- Never show raw error codes or stack traces

### 1.7 Dashboard Design Patterns

Dashboards are the crown jewel of this product. Every dashboard must feel like opening Bloomberg Terminal meets Stripe Dashboard — dense with information yet beautifully organized.

**Stat Cards (KPI Cards):**
- Icon (in brand-tinted circle bg) + Label (text-sm gray-500) + Value (text-3xl font-bold) + Trend indicator (green up arrow or red down arrow + percentage)
- Values animate counting up from 0 on page load
- Subtle gradient border on hover
- Grid: 4 columns on desktop, 2 on tablet, 1 on mobile

**Charts:**
- Use a consistent chart library (Recharts or Nivo) across all dashboards
- Color palette: use the accent palette defined above, never random colors
- All charts must have: title, optional subtitle, legend, tooltip on hover, responsive sizing
- Animate on enter (lines draw, bars grow up, pie segments rotate in)
- Include a time range selector (Today, This Week, This Month, This Term, This Year, Custom)
- Chart types to implement:
  - Area charts for trends over time (attendance, enrollment, fee collection)
  - Bar charts for comparisons (grade distribution, section performance)
  - Donut charts for composition (student demographics, fee status breakdown)
  - Line charts for multi-series trends (performance across subjects)
  - Heatmaps for attendance patterns (days × weeks)
  - Sparklines inline in tables/cards for quick trends

**Dashboard Layout:**
- Top: Welcome banner with user name, date, school name, and quick action buttons
- Row 1: 4 KPI stat cards
- Row 2: 2-column layout — primary chart (2/3 width) + secondary info (1/3 width)
- Row 3: Full-width table or activity feed
- Row 4: Additional charts or widgets in 2-3 column grid
- Use CSS Grid with responsive breakpoints, never let content feel cramped

