## PART 8 — INTERACTION PATTERNS AND MICRO-INTERACTIONS

### 8.1 Must-Have Micro-Interactions

1. **Sidebar Navigation:** Active item has a brand-colored left border (3px) and brand-50 background. Hover shows subtle bg change. Collapse/expand with smooth width transition. Tooltips appear on collapsed icons.

2. **Table Row Hover:** Subtle gray-50 background, slight shadow lift, action buttons fade in on the right.

3. **Button Press:** Scale down to 0.98 on tap, spring back. Primary buttons get a subtle glow ring on focus.

4. **Card Hover:** Lift up 2px with shadow-md transition. Slight border color change to brand-200.

5. **Toggle Switch:** Smooth slide with spring physics. Color transition from gray to brand. Satisfying haptic feel through animation.

6. **Notification Bell:** Bounce animation when new notification arrives. Badge count animates in with scale spring.

7. **Status Badge Dot:** Gentle pulse animation on "Live" or "Active" indicators.

8. **Form Validation:** Input border smoothly transitions to green (valid) or red (invalid). Error message slides down from below the field. Success checkmark fades in at the right of the input.

9. **Data Loading:** Skeleton screens that perfectly mirror the actual layout. Shimmer effect left-to-right. Content fades in when loaded.

10. **Page Transitions:** Subtle fade + slide-up when navigating between pages. Breadcrumb updates with animation.

11. **Stat Counter Animation:** Numbers count up from 0 when they enter the viewport. Use easeOut curve for natural deceleration.

12. **Chart Animations:** Lines draw progressively. Bars grow from bottom. Pie/donut segments rotate in. Tooltips appear with fade + scale.

13. **Modal Entrance:** Backdrop fades in. Modal scales up from 0.95 with fade. Exit reverses.

14. **Toast Notifications:** Slide in from the right. Auto-dismiss with progress bar. Stack multiple toasts with 8px gap.

15. **Drag and Drop (Kanban, Timetable):** Dragged item lifts with shadow. Drop zone highlights. Smooth reorder animation. Placeholder shows insertion point.

16. **Search/Command Palette:** Full overlay with blur backdrop. Results appear as you type with slight fade. Keyboard navigation with highlighted row.

17. **Avatar Loading:** Blurred placeholder → sharp image fade transition.

18. **Empty State Illustration:** SVG illustration with subtle floating animation (up-down 4px, 3s cycle).

19. **Progress Steps (Multi-step forms):** Active step scales up slightly. Completed steps show checkmark with celebration micro-animation. Connector line fills with brand color.

20. **Tab Switching:** Active tab indicator slides horizontally with spring physics. Content cross-fades.

### 8.2 Responsive Breakpoints

```
Mobile:      < 640px    → Single column, bottom nav, full-width cards
Tablet:      640-1024px → Collapsed sidebar, 2-column grids, stacked layouts
Desktop:     1024-1440px → Full sidebar, 3-4 column grids, side-by-side panels
Large:       > 1440px   → Centered content (max 1440px), larger cards, more breathing room
```

### 8.3 Accessibility Requirements

- All interactive elements keyboard accessible
- Focus rings visible (brand-500, 2px offset)
- Color contrast ratio minimum 4.5:1 for text
- Screen reader labels on all icons and interactive elements
- Alt text on all images
- Form fields properly labeled with aria attributes
- Error messages programmatically associated with fields
- Skip to content link
- Reduced motion support (respect prefers-reduced-motion)
- Minimum touch target 44x44px on mobile

### 8.4 Empty, Loading, and Error State Standards

**Every page and data-displaying component MUST have all three states:**

**Loading State:**
- Skeleton screen matching the exact layout of the loaded state
- Shimmer animation (gradient sweep left to right)
- Never show a centered spinner alone — always show layout structure
- Minimum display time: 300ms (prevent flash of loading state)

**Empty State:**
- Centered in the content area
- Custom SVG illustration (light, brand-colored, 120-160px)
- Heading: "No [items] yet" in text-lg semibold
- Description: One sentence explaining what this section does
- CTA button: "Add First [Item]" or "Get Started"
- Example empty states:
  - Students: "Your student directory is empty. Start by adding your first student or importing from a file."
  - Attendance: "No attendance recorded for today. Select a class to begin marking attendance."
  - Invoices: "No invoices generated yet. Create a fee structure first, then generate invoices."

**Error State:**
- Red-tinted illustration or icon
- "Something went wrong" heading
- Brief description of what failed
- "Try Again" button
- "Contact Support" link for persistent errors
- Log error details to console (not shown to user)

