## PART 10 — CRITICAL IMPLEMENTATION RULES

1. **Use mock data that looks 100% real.** No "John Doe" or "Test Student". Use realistic Arabic, Indian, Pakistani, British, Filipino names. Realistic Emirates IDs, phone numbers (+971), addresses in Dubai neighborhoods (Al Barsha, Jumeirah, Silicon Oasis, Marina, Downtown).

2. **Every chart must animate on load.** No static charts appearing instantly. Lines draw, bars grow, numbers count up.

3. **Every table must have search, filters, pagination, and export.** No table appears without these four features.

4. **Every form must validate in real-time.** No "submit and see errors" pattern. Validate each field on blur, show inline errors immediately.

5. **Navigation must feel instant.** Use skeleton loading, not blank white pages. Show the layout structure immediately while data loads.

6. **Color must carry meaning.** Green = positive/active/present. Red = negative/overdue/absent. Amber = warning/pending/late. Blue = info/in-progress. Purple = brand accent.

7. **Typography hierarchy must be immediately clear.** Page title (text-2xl bold) → Section title (text-lg semibold) → Card title (text-base semibold) → Body (text-sm normal) → Caption (text-xs gray-500).

8. **Whitespace is a design element.** Never cram content. Use generous padding (24px card padding, 32px page padding). Let content breathe.

9. **Every interactive element must have a hover state, focus state, active state, and disabled state.** No exceptions.

10. **Dark mode is NOT required for MVP.** Focus on a perfect light theme first.

11. **Sidebar must show the current school name and logo, current academic year, and current user avatar and role.**

12. **Every page must have a page header with: breadcrumb, page title, and relevant action buttons (Add New, Export, Filter).**

13. **Toast notifications for every action:** "Student added successfully ✓", "Attendance saved ✓", "Payment recorded ✓"

14. **Confirmation dialogs for destructive actions:** "Are you sure you want to deactivate this student? This action can be reversed by an administrator."

15. **The login page must be stunning.** Full-screen split layout. Left: school image with gradient overlay and a powerful tagline. Right: clean login form with the school group logo.

16. **Financial numbers must use proper formatting.** AED 45,250.00 (with currency code), percentages with one decimal (94.7%), counts with comma separators (3,200).

17. **Dates in DD MMM YYYY format** (21 Oct 2026) for readability. Times in 12-hour format (8:30 AM).

18. **The product must work on iPad in landscape orientation** — this is how many principals and teachers will use it.

19. **Build a notification bell that actually shows realistic notifications** with timestamps ("5 minutes ago", "2 hours ago", "Yesterday").

20. **The command palette (Cmd+K) must be implemented** with categories: Pages, Students, Staff, Actions, Recent.

